The patch now keeps the existing `tokens` record unchanged, adds `codex_tokens`, and shares the same path→byte-offset file across both sources. I’ve also kept source isolation: Claude and Codex transcript failures are handled independently, and individual damaged files/lines remain non-fatal. Next I’m running the real pulse and comparing its emitted record with the prior one.
